<BaseLayout title="Privacy" activePage="privacy" description="How reading preferences and optional YouTube playback work on The False Positive.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <h2 id="music">Music and YouTube</h2>
  <p>The site attempts to start background music at 10% volume when you arrive and the page is visible. If your browser blocks automatic sound, the site tries once more when you first click outside the music tools. You can also use Play in the music controls. Unless you paused music earlier in this browser session, this connects to YouTube automatically. The player loads from the privacy-enhanced domain youtube-nocookie.com; its control script loads from youtube.com. The video is kept offscreen; YouTube still supplies the underlying video stream.</p>
  <p>Loading the player sends connection information, such as your IP address and browser information, to YouTube. YouTube may collect playback information, store information on your device, and show advertisements. Privacy-enhanced mode limits personalization; it does not make playback anonymous.</p>
  <p>The music feature uses YouTube API Services. By using it, you agree to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>. Read the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> for details about YouTube’s data practices.</p>
  <p>This site does not request your YouTube account, login credentials, or permission to access your account. Closing the Music panel leaves playback running. Use Pause to stop listening. Music continues while you navigate between site pages. Leaving the browser tab pauses playback at its current position. Returning resumes the same song unless you paused it yourself.</p>
  <h2>Preferences stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>Reading settings are saved in your browser’s local storage. Your music pause choice, volume, selected song and playback position, dismissal of the music-controls tip, and writeup wave-motion choice are saved for the current browser session. These preferences are not sent to a server by the site. You can reset reading settings in the tools menu or remove saved preferences through your browser’s site-data controls.</p>
  <h2>Other external services</h2>
  <p>The site loads fonts and icons from Google Fonts and cdnjs. The News page uses an external RSS service. Requests to these services share connection information with their providers. External links open websites with their own privacy practices.</p>
  <p>For questions, use the contact links on the <a href="/about">About page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
